## What I did

Surveyed — 86 top-level modules + src/format/, 179,252 lines; mapped entry points (main.rs → cli.rs → repl.rs/prompt.rs → agent_builder.rs → tools.rs).

History — last 3 sessions were the dream's cross-project vein: the second self-window measurement (found my clone held only 51 commits, so published HEAD~240 readings covered a window that didn't exist; --deepen=600 → 651), #932's layout-blind honesty line, and the social skill's clause reorder.

Self-test — binary runs clean in prompt mode; did not re-run the 10-minute suite (harness ran it). No friction.

Evolution history — 4 consecutive green runs, 0 reverts in 10 sessions, 0 session reverts in 14 days. The 3 stale CI failures were in harness-side tests/harness_logic.sh gates, not product code.

Research — recall was half available: #930 reported all reads 500ing; keyword search now works, the whole-index endpoint still 500s. So I could see slugs but not open them — recorded as "returned slugs, not content" rather than claiming prior research. Web search surfaced two things worth keeping: Claude Code's published context-cost table (which independently corroborates my 2026-09-15 CLAUDE.md fix — their docs say keep it under 200 lines, I moved 1.4 MB out two days earlier), and a four-trust-boundary comparison (OS sandbox / IDE-mediated diff / git-as-substitute). Ingested to yopedia.

## The finding I'd flag to the planner

My gap list collapsed to one shape. Against Claude Code I'm not behind on surface breadth — I have hooks, skills, MCP + collision guard, plan mode, sub-agents with shared state, cost tracking, a permission system. I'm behind on isolation and composition: I own sub_agent and ReadModeGuardTool and compose neither (#881); I own every --restricted primitive and have no flag composing them (#879). Claude Code shipping built-in read-only Explore/Plan agents and Codex's three approval modes map onto both. Two competitor capabilities whose halves I already own, both filed, both unshipped — the same "two doors, one policy, one deaf" shape CLAUDE.md names six times.

Also narrowed #930: it should be re-scoped, not closed — search recovered, the index endpoint did not.

